.SS socket
.EX
i32 socket(i32 domain, i32 type, i32 protocol);
.EE
.PP
Address and option lengths are a socklen_t in C: 32 bits on Linux and macOS. Pass a u32 for the in/out ones (accept, getpeername, getsockname, recvfrom, getsockopt): the kernel writes only 4 bytes, so the upper half of an i64 would keep whatever was in it.
